Here’s the **complete setup** for monitoring **Pod Start Time**, which helps you identify **when a pod was last deployed or restarted**.

---

## 🕓 **Pod Start Time Alert (Unix Timestamp)**

---

### ✅ 1. Main Query (Prometheus)

```prometheus
kube_pod_start_time{
  cluster_name="azure-eastus-st-085-np-aks-001",
  namespace="storefront-storefront-ut",
  pod=~"storefront-api-ut-.*"
}
```

> This returns the **start time of each pod** as a Unix timestamp. It updates when the pod restarts or is recreated.

---

### 🚨 2. Alert Query Setup (for detecting recent restarts)

You likely want to alert if a pod has **started within the last X minutes** (e.g., 5 minutes = potential restart).

---

### ✅ Alert Query (calculate pod uptime in minutes)

```prometheus
(time() - kube_pod_start_time{
  cluster_name="azure-eastus-st-085-np-aks-001",
  namespace="storefront-storefront-ut",
  pod=~"storefront-api-ut-.*"
}) / 60
```

---

### 🚨 Alert Rule Setup (Grafana Unified Alerting)

| Setting            | Value                                                             |
| ------------------ | ----------------------------------------------------------------- |
| **Query A**        | Use the alert query above                                         |
| **Expression B**   | `Reduce` → Function: `Min` or `Max` → Input: `A`                  |
| **Expression C**   | `Threshold` → Input: `B`, Condition: `IS BELOW`, Value: `5`       |
| **Evaluate every** | `3m`                                                              |
| **For (pending)**  | `1m`                                                              |
| **Alert name**     | `Pod Recently Started`                                            |
| **Folder**         | `MOBILITY_OPERATIONS_STOREFRONT-nonProd`                          |
| **Labels**         | `alert_type: pod_start_time`, `environment: ut`, `severity: info` |

---

### 📝 3. Description (for Alert)

```yaml
summary: "Pod recently started in storefront-storefront-ut"
description: |
  One or more pods in namespace `storefront-storefront-ut` were started 
  within the last 5 minutes in cluster `azure-eastus-st-085-np-aks-001`. 
  This may be expected (e.g., rollout), or may indicate unexpected restarts. 
  Review deployment timelines and container logs if unplanned.
```

